### Import each curl from README into Postman, or use this with IntelliJ HTTP Client.
@base = http://localhost:8080
@product = 11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111
@success = 22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222222
@failure = 33333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333333

### Product list
GET {{base}}/products

### Create product (inventory is a separate bounded context; this does not provision stock)
POST {{base}}/products
Content-Type: application/json

{"name":"Training Book","price":29.95}

### Update seed product
PUT {{base}}/products/{{product}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"name":"Training Laptop","price":999.00}

### Read stock
GET {{base}}/inventory/{{product}}

### Success (repeating the same key/body returns the same order)
POST {{base}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: {{success}}
X-Correlation-ID: day7-success

{"productId":"{{product}}","quantity":2,"failPayment":false}

### Poll until CONFIRMED
GET {{base}}/orders/{{success}}

### Deliberate payment failure
POST {{base}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: {{failure}}
X-Correlation-ID: day7-failure

{"productId":"{{product}}","quantity":3,"failPayment":true}

### Poll until CANCELLED; stock should have been restored
GET {{base}}/orders/{{failure}}

### Notifications
GET {{base}}/notifications/{{failure}}

### Payment result
GET {{base}}/payments/{{failure}}

### Standalone reservation (do not use an active saga's order ID)
POST {{base}}/inventory/reservations
Content-Type: application/json

{"orderId":"44444444-4444-4444-4444-444444444444","productId":"{{product}}","quantity":1}

### Idempotent release
DELETE {{base}}/inventory/reservations/44444444-4444-4444-4444-444444444444

### Liveness
GET http://localhost:8083/actuator/health/liveness

### Readiness
GET http://localhost:8083/actuator/health/readiness
